From c7f65355ebd788c705ef6dddd6030bab679f7791 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adhemerval Zanella <adhemerval.zanella@linaro.org>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:32:38 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] math: Sync erfc with CORE-MATH ac1993d8 (BZ 35052)

It syncs with CORE-MATH up to commit ac1993d8, which brings the fix
from commit 9dc99d96 for a spurious underflow exception.  For inputs
slightly below 0x1.9db1bb14e15cap+4, the computation in
erfc_asympt_fast raises underflow although the result (around 2^-970)
is a normal number.

The new tests are the erfc worst-case inputs that CORE-MATH added for
this issue (commit 3822ff89).

Checked on x86_64-linux-gnu, aarch64-linux-gnu, and
powerpc64le-linux-gnu.

Reviewed-by: Paul Zimmermann <Paul.Zimmermann@inria.fr>
(cherry picked from commit 655640eba70c68de0b203a0e0c90852533c155e8)
---
 NEWS                            |   1 +
 SHARED-FILES                    |   2 +-
 math/auto-libm-test-in          |   6 +
 math/auto-libm-test-out-erfc    | 345 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 sysdeps/ieee754/dbl-64/s_erfc.c |  19 +-
 5 files changed, 370 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/NEWS b/NEWS
index d870637e8359..35f7d8648725 100644
--- a/NEWS
+++ b/NEWS
@@ -97,6 +97,7 @@ The following bugs are resolved with this release:
     (CVE-2026-100290)
   [34993] glob: double free in prefix_array after a memory allocation
     failure (CVE-2026-126765)
+  [35052] math: erfc raises spurious underflow
   [35053] math: math: lgammaf@GLIBC_2.23 writes to signgam since 2.43
 
 Version 2.44
